From: Vinay Adella <vadella@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 11:42:13 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] iw: increase netlink socket rx buffer size for parallel scan

With WIPHY_FLAG_SUPPORTS_PARALLEL_HW_SCAN enabled, two concurrent scans
on different radios complete nearly simultaneously and the kernel delivers
two NL80211_CMD_NEW_SCAN_RESULTS multicast events in rapid succession.
The subsequent NL80211_CMD_GET_SCAN dump also returns BSS entries from
both radios in one shot.

The hardcoded 8192 byte rx buffer is too small to hold the combined scan
results, causing nl_recvmsgs() to return ENOBUFS (-105) and the scan
results to be lost.

Increase the rx buffer to 1 MB, matching what wpa_supplicant and hostapd
use for the same reason.

Signed-off-by: Vinay Adella <vadella@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 iw.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/iw.c
+++ b/iw.c
@@ -61,7 +61,8 @@ static int nl80211_init(struct nl80211_state *state)
 		goto out_handle_destroy;
 	}

-	nl_socket_set_buffer_size(state->nl_sock, 8192, 8192);
+	/* Increase rx buffer to 1 MB to handle parallel scan results */
+	nl_socket_set_buffer_size(state->nl_sock, 1024 * 1024, 8192);

 	/* try to set NETLINK_EXT_ACK to 1, ignoring errors */
 	err = 1;
